Subject: [PATCH 13/22] fixup! Wave 1, taps: a second tap does one thing; the
 menu, its search and the ways back

fixup! Wave 1, taps: a second tap does one thing; the menu, its search and the ways back

The open menu locks the root only, so the top bar (the cross, the page's name) stays on screen on a scrolled page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FKTjPFbzEx2ZvP4BhqKEiS
---
 core/ui/base.css | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/ui/base.css b/core/ui/base.css
index 6cc137e..170298c 100644
--- a/core/ui/base.css
+++ b/core/ui/base.css
@@ -77,7 +77,9 @@ p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
   #sidebar { visibility: hidden; overscroll-behavior: contain; transition: transform .18s ease, visibility 0s linear .18s; }
   #sidebar.open { visibility: visible; transition: transform .18s ease, visibility 0s; }
   #scrim { touch-action: none; }
-  html.drawer-open, html.drawer-open body { overflow: hidden; }
+  /* the root only: locked on body too, body becomes its own scroller and the sticky top bar (the cross, the page's name)
+     sticks to the top of the page, scrolled out of view (tapmenu new problem 1) */
+  html.drawer-open { overflow: hidden; }
   html.drawer-open #topbar { touch-action: none; }
 }
 @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { #sidebar, .nav-group-head .chev { transition: none !important; } }
